{
  "requirement": "Habeas uses the TBV [outline selector grammar](sdk/outlines.md#parse-an-outline-selector)\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.selector_syntax` for source addresses.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has one obligation: Habeas uses the TBV outline selector grammar, as defined by `requirements.sdk.outlines.selector_syntax`, for source addresses. That requirement is cited as context, so I checked that the tests apply its grammar to Habeas addresses. I did not reassess its own tests.\n\nThe marked tests cover the grammar as follows:\n- **Rust paths and encoding:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/tests.rs#fn[rust_selectors_follow_syntactic_ancestry]` checks `/`-separated paths and the empty selector resolving to the root. It checks `kind[name]` segments, the multipart `impl[Thing/Trait]`, and percent-encoding in `impl[%5Bu8;%204%5D]`. It also checks `#1` and `#2` disambiguators, and that an ambiguous `fn[repeated]` and a missing selector both fail to resolve.\n- **Anonymous hashes:** `fn[anonymous_selectors_use_identity_hashes]` checks the `use@` plus 12 hex digits form, that selectors survive an insertion, and that they fail after a content change. It also checks `#N` for duplicate anonymous nodes.\n- **Line nodes:** `fn[plain_text_lines_are_interchangeable_anonymous_nodes]` checks that identical `line@` selectors are equal and resolve, and that whitespace is normalised.\n- **Anonymous containers:** `fn[anonymous_container_selectors_use_identity_hashes_and_survive_descendant_edits]` checks the `kind@hash` form for containers, built from the identity hash. It also checks stability when a descendant is edited, and that a child path continues from the anonymous segment.\n- **Markdown:** `src/outline/markdown_tests.rs#fn[paragraphs_and_nested_directives_have_independent_source_ranges]` checks the `kind@` plus 12 digit segment form, and that every selector resolves back to its node.\n- **Errors:** `fn[profile_rules_map_only_matching_contexts_and_keep_other_nodes_transparent]` checks the missing-selector error and the invalid-selector error for a malformed percent escape.\n- **Habeas source addresses:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/search.rs#fn[outline_addresses_validate_selectors_without_reading_paths]` checks that `OutlineData::new` accepts `\"\"`, `fn[kept]` and `mod[a%2Fb]/fn[kept]`. It also checks that it rejects `fn[missing`, `fn[bad%ZZ]` and a leading `/`, and that this does not depend on the path.\n\nI found no accepted-but-wrong behaviour. Other Habeas tests exercise the same resolution path, for example `tests/evidence_boundaries.rs` and `tests/authoring_cli.rs`. They carry no `{test}` reference to this requirement, but the marked tests already cover the grammar, so I did not treat that as a gap.",
  "references": "2c6fb45ec8a367d6739dd65005439f9370f78d69a364f7f23056d35dcb5f7f73",
